WEBVTT

00:00.970 --> 00:04.980
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:05.000 --> 00:08.220
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:08.259 --> 00:11.640
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.660 --> 00:14.440
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.470 --> 00:18.100
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.120 --> 00:21.540
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.570 --> 00:23.160
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.180 --> 00:24.560
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.651 --> 00:30.080
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.860 --> 00:38.530
Peter, come on.

00:38.580 --> 00:39.940
- What?
- We're starting.

00:39.960 --> 00:41.400
Oh, is this, uh, a new one?

00:41.420 --> 00:43.380
I thought it was a rerun.
Okay, here we go.

00:43.420 --> 00:45.610
Line?

00:45.650 --> 00:48.110
What are those guys doing over there?

00:48.120 --> 00:49.860
Hey, what are those
guys doing over there?

00:49.900 --> 00:51.700
I added a "hey."

00:51.720 --> 00:54.370
Here we go, Patriots!

00:54.410 --> 00:56.140
All right, now let's go miss the urinal

00:56.170 --> 00:57.869
with half a whiz and get out of here.

00:57.870 --> 00:59.219
Right on!

00:59.220 --> 01:00.230
Hey, why you guys leaving?

01:00.250 --> 01:02.060
We're taking a party bus to the game.

01:02.120 --> 01:03.830
A bus for partying?

01:03.880 --> 01:05.280
Aw, that sounds awesome.

01:05.300 --> 01:07.140
Like a pair of Pete's Headphones.

01:07.170 --> 01:09.600
♪ Oye c├│mo va ♪

01:09.680 --> 01:10.960
♪ Mi ritmo ♪

01:10.990 --> 01:13.550
♪ Bueno pa' gozar ♪

01:13.590 --> 01:14.599
♪ Mulata ♪

01:14.600 --> 01:16.600
♪ Ba, ba-da ba-da-da ♪

01:16.640 --> 01:18.350
♪ Ba-da-da-da-da-da ♪

01:18.390 --> 01:21.900
♪ Da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da... ♪

01:24.650 --> 01:26.419
Mom, can we eat?

01:26.420 --> 01:29.110
My stomach is starting to sound
like Arnold Schwarzenegger

01:29.150 --> 01:31.900
gasping for air at the
end of Total Recall.

01:31.990 --> 01:34.260
My eyes are

01:34.280 --> 01:36.780
popping out at the end of this movie!

01:36.830 --> 01:38.740
Well, I'd like to wait for your father.

01:38.770 --> 01:41.859
L-Let me send him another
infuriating check-in text.

01:41.860 --> 01:44.180
Hel-lo!

01:44.330 --> 01:45.790
Yes?

01:45.840 --> 01:47.620
Peter, where the hell have you been?

01:47.650 --> 01:50.600
On a magical journey to
Gillette Stadium and back.

01:50.630 --> 01:52.330
You remember last night
when you called me

01:52.340 --> 01:54.680
the lowest-class alcoholic in the world?

01:54.720 --> 01:58.220
Well, I found one rung lower.
I'm a party bus guy now.

01:58.260 --> 02:00.960
That's got to be way better
than when I drove a Fiat.

02:00.990 --> 02:03.430
Hey! You cut me off!

02:03.480 --> 02:05.600
What? Turn down your radio.

02:05.650 --> 02:08.280
I can't. My stomach's pressed
up against the dial.

02:08.300 --> 02:09.480
You want to go?

02:09.500 --> 02:12.260
Get me 17 shoehorns and some canola oil,

02:12.270 --> 02:13.340
and we'll go!

02:13.580 --> 02:16.360
Get back here!

02:19.170 --> 02:22.330
Okay, guys, now this is a bus
for a fireman's bachelor party.

02:22.370 --> 02:24.680
So just follow my lead
and we'll fit right in.

02:24.720 --> 02:26.710
All right!

02:26.750 --> 02:28.790
9/11! Boston Strong!

02:28.840 --> 02:29.920
Never forget!

02:29.930 --> 02:31.820
How about this guy? You forget?

02:31.850 --> 02:34.970
No way. You're too Boston
Strong to ever forget.

02:35.010 --> 02:37.060
Let's roll!

02:37.140 --> 02:40.839
Uh, I mean... civil servants
with hero complexes!

02:40.840 --> 02:41.900
Boom!

02:41.920 --> 02:44.500
- All right!
- Welcome, other firefighters.

02:44.520 --> 02:47.240
Bring us the man of the hour.

02:47.260 --> 02:48.650
Come on, Smitty!

02:50.820 --> 02:53.730
To my last night as a free man!

02:57.240 --> 02:59.530
Hmm. Unfortunate timing.

02:59.580 --> 03:01.410
Now, which one of these scumbag firemen

03:01.450 --> 03:03.120
will go after his fianc├йe?

03:03.200 --> 03:05.450
Already happened. We're very happy.

03:08.620 --> 03:13.250
♪ Firemen are not good friends ♪

03:13.300 --> 03:17.760
♪ They'll bang your wife
when you are dead. ♪

03:22.930 --> 03:25.099
Peter, this sucks!

03:25.100 --> 03:26.920
What are we doing out here?

03:27.880 --> 03:29.460
_

03:39.320 --> 03:41.550
I'm beginning to think
those vodka cranberries

03:41.580 --> 03:43.560
may have had alcohol in them.

03:49.360 --> 03:52.000
Wow, partying on the bus to prom.

03:52.040 --> 03:54.040
Doesn't get much cooler than this.

03:54.090 --> 03:56.260
None of these lame kids is drinking.

03:56.280 --> 03:59.120
Eh, I think I know what's going on.

03:59.390 --> 04:02.720
Hey, how many of you kids
are on the horny drugs?

04:04.000 --> 04:05.430
I'm a cop.

04:06.640 --> 04:08.600
But I'm not a narc.

04:10.300 --> 04:12.300
Cool cop! Cool cop! Cool cop!

04:12.400 --> 04:14.900
Did you dook yourself?

04:14.940 --> 04:17.070
Just listen to the chant, Peter.

04:17.110 --> 04:19.420
Listen to the chant.

04:21.460 --> 04:24.320
_

04:26.790 --> 04:29.040
Close dancing, 12 o'clock.

04:29.080 --> 04:31.920
Hey, arm's length, dirty porno lovers!

04:31.960 --> 04:34.210
So, going stag tonight, Meg?

04:34.250 --> 04:37.000
Oh, no, I brought someone.

04:37.050 --> 04:39.380
Hello. I'm in love with Meg.

04:39.430 --> 04:42.010
Well, now I'm very sorry I asked.

04:42.100 --> 04:44.430
Wow, the end of high school.

04:44.470 --> 04:47.170
Tonight, we pass around Stifler's mom,

04:47.180 --> 04:49.980
and in the morning, it's off
to die quick in Vietnam.

04:50.020 --> 04:52.280
Peter, I think you're getting
your movies mixed up.

04:52.290 --> 04:54.180
Attention, students.

04:54.200 --> 04:57.270
It's time to announce this
year's prom king and queen.

04:57.320 --> 04:58.980
Natalee Holloway!

04:58.990 --> 05:01.380
Now, now.

05:01.390 --> 05:02.990
And the winners are...

05:03.030 --> 05:06.780
Connie D'Amico and "Kermit Legs" Kyle!

05:09.220 --> 05:11.290
Ah, so close.

05:12.290 --> 05:13.880
Hello, gorgeous.

05:13.890 --> 05:15.719
- How old are you?
- 18.

05:15.720 --> 05:17.780
All right, and I just
recorded you saying that.

05:17.800 --> 05:19.960
And hi. I am Glenn Quagmire.

05:19.970 --> 05:21.630
Courtney. Nice to meet you.

05:21.680 --> 05:23.959
You don't look like
you're in high school.

05:23.960 --> 05:26.930
I got held back. You
like getting held back?

05:26.970 --> 05:29.220
Sometimes.

05:33.440 --> 05:34.660
All right, youngins.

05:34.670 --> 05:37.550
I dragged this piece of dirty
cardboard in from the alley

05:37.560 --> 05:39.650
to show y'all how to get down.

05:39.690 --> 05:41.650
Peter! Let's boogie!

05:46.160 --> 05:48.160
♪ Ho! Ho! ♪

06:14.560 --> 06:16.870
Aah! There was a staple in the box!

06:16.880 --> 06:18.940
Where's the nurse's office?

06:18.980 --> 06:21.390
Hey, you want to get out of here?

06:21.400 --> 06:23.650
Yeah. Let's go.

06:23.780 --> 06:25.480
You take requests?

06:25.490 --> 06:27.660
What are you looking for?

06:27.700 --> 06:30.240
♪ A-hunga, hunga, hunga, hunga... ♪

06:31.700 --> 06:34.940
♪ It's been one week
since you looked at me ♪

06:34.960 --> 06:37.560
♪ Cocked your head to the
side and said I'm angry ♪

06:37.580 --> 06:39.330
♪ Five days since you laughed at me... ♪

06:39.380 --> 06:40.520
I know all the lyrics.

06:40.550 --> 06:42.550
- I just don't know them fast!
- ♪ Three days... ♪

06:45.020 --> 06:47.700
- And initial here.
- What is all this?

06:47.720 --> 06:49.390
Oh, these just say if anything
should happen to you,

06:49.430 --> 06:51.200
I'm not responsible, blah-blah-blah.

06:51.220 --> 06:52.560
I'm-I'm just boring myself.

06:52.600 --> 06:54.920
I had a lot of fun with
you tonight, Courtney.

06:54.930 --> 06:56.690
Me too.

06:56.730 --> 06:58.480
Oh, Courtney.

06:58.520 --> 06:59.810
Oh, Glenn.

06:59.860 --> 07:02.360
Oh, oh, giggity!

07:02.400 --> 07:05.920
Wait. Did you just say "giggity"?

07:05.930 --> 07:07.420
Yeah. Sorry.

07:07.440 --> 07:09.920
Sometimes I just blurt that
out when I get excited.

07:09.930 --> 07:11.900
Oh, my God. Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

07:11.940 --> 07:14.160
_

07:15.440 --> 07:18.060
Here. Rub this up and down
on the inside of your cheek.

07:18.080 --> 07:20.120
- Giggity.
- Aah! Stop saying that!

07:23.380 --> 07:24.920
_

07:26.420 --> 07:28.160
What is it, Glenn? What's wrong?

07:28.260 --> 07:31.300
You're... you're my daughter!

07:31.350 --> 07:32.880
Oh, my God!

07:32.890 --> 07:34.180
Wow.

07:34.220 --> 07:37.100
I guess this means I have
a phone call to make.

07:37.140 --> 07:39.000
Hey, it's Glenn Quagmire.

07:39.020 --> 07:41.800
Would you tell Andrew that
he is not the father?

07:41.820 --> 07:44.659
Andrew, you are not the father.

08:02.060 --> 08:04.730
Courtney, there's something
I just got to ask.

08:04.770 --> 08:07.260
What the heck was the
theme of that dance?

08:07.300 --> 08:08.680
- What do you mean?
- I mean, like,

08:08.690 --> 08:10.930
there was palm trees like it was Hawaii,

08:10.940 --> 08:13.240
but then there was a suit
of armor in the corner.

08:13.260 --> 08:15.480
There was a big banner
w-with fish on it.

08:15.520 --> 08:18.020
Can we get back to the
fact that you're my dad?

08:18.070 --> 08:20.350
Yeah, you're right.
I'm-I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

08:20.360 --> 08:23.450
Well, let me ask. What's
up with your mom?

08:23.490 --> 08:25.700
Actually, I never knew my mom.

08:25.740 --> 08:28.740
I was hoping that you
could tell me about her.

08:28.790 --> 08:31.330
Uh... of course I can.

08:31.370 --> 08:32.830
Your mom...

08:32.870 --> 08:36.340
your mom... was really...

08:36.440 --> 08:38.920
thing hanging on the
bulletin board behind you.

08:38.960 --> 08:41.720
That's so nice to hear. Tell me more.

08:41.740 --> 08:44.760
Oh, gosh, she was, she was just so...

08:44.780 --> 08:46.740
word on the bottom of your coffee cup.

08:46.760 --> 08:49.540
I always knew she would be! What else?

08:49.570 --> 08:51.730
I just have some great
memories of her...

08:51.770 --> 08:53.980
numbers to call in case of emergency

08:54.000 --> 08:55.400
or accidental poisoning.

08:55.520 --> 08:58.480
It's like she's here with us right now.

08:58.530 --> 09:01.150
So you don't know your
mom? Who do you live with?

09:01.190 --> 09:03.340
Well, right now I'm on a futon

09:03.360 --> 09:05.000
in the rafters of my friend's garage.

09:05.010 --> 09:07.340
Oh! Actually, I better get going.

09:07.370 --> 09:09.480
I have to feed their
ferrets. They breed them.

09:09.490 --> 09:11.870
It's pretty terrifying.

09:11.910 --> 09:15.140
Anyway, thank you so
much for being so nice,

09:15.160 --> 09:17.420
and let's talk soon?

09:17.460 --> 09:19.919
Wait, hold on. You can't
live in a ferret garage.

09:19.920 --> 09:20.930
You need a home.

09:21.060 --> 09:23.610
You know, you could move in here.

09:23.650 --> 09:26.340
I have an extra bedroom,
and the bed has a bunch

09:26.360 --> 09:28.070
of different-sized pillows on it.

09:28.110 --> 09:31.300
Hmm. I do love dealing with
those pillows every day,

09:31.320 --> 09:33.060
but are you sure?

09:33.100 --> 09:34.410
I don't want to be a burden.

09:34.450 --> 09:37.370
No, it's no problem.
Hey, you're my daughter.

09:37.410 --> 09:39.540
I want to make sure you
have everything you need.

09:39.580 --> 09:42.370
Thanks. That's sweet.

09:42.380 --> 09:46.000
Um... okay! Yeah. I'll move in.

09:46.050 --> 09:47.460
That's huge for me.

09:47.600 --> 09:49.880
Hey, is that an Instant Pot?

09:49.930 --> 09:52.770
- No, it's a Crock-Pot.
- You got to get an Instant Pot.

09:52.800 --> 09:54.630
You can make short ribs in
it. It falls right off...

09:54.640 --> 09:56.280
Yeah, yeah, falls right
off the bone. I know.

09:56.290 --> 09:57.860
I've had this conversation five times.

09:57.880 --> 09:59.470
Hey, Quagmire.

09:59.480 --> 10:01.740
I hear you're considering
an Instant Pot.

10:01.840 --> 10:03.980
Courtney, that's Joe, my neighbor.

10:04.070 --> 10:07.280
Hey, Courtney. You getting
this guy on board?

10:10.140 --> 10:13.660
So, I think I had a wet
nightmare last night.

10:13.700 --> 10:14.960
Is that possible?

10:15.000 --> 10:18.000
- Hello, fellow daddios.
- Did you bang your kid yet?

10:18.060 --> 10:20.590
Okay, Peter, can I talk
to you for a second?

10:20.680 --> 10:23.680
I'm sorry, but I am not going
to stand for any misogyny.

10:23.730 --> 10:25.560
Stop acting like a Neanderthal pig.

10:25.600 --> 10:27.510
Those sound scary.

10:27.520 --> 10:29.690
What were you two ladies talking about?

10:29.730 --> 10:32.070
Joe, can I talk to you for a second?

10:32.110 --> 10:35.540
It's 2019. Time-tested jokes like that

10:35.570 --> 10:37.280
are now offensive and not funny at all.

10:38.860 --> 10:40.030
Okay, I got to go.

10:40.080 --> 10:42.620
I'm taking Courtney to
her first WNBA game.

10:42.630 --> 10:44.290
I got courtside seats.

10:44.330 --> 10:46.660
They're way in the back, but
I'm sitting next to Courtney.

10:46.710 --> 10:49.040
I-I got dad jokes now.

10:49.090 --> 10:51.080
See you, friends.

10:51.300 --> 10:52.920
Yes, 911?

10:52.960 --> 10:55.470
Someone has stolen the old Quagmire

10:55.510 --> 10:59.300
and replaced him with a respectable man.

10:59.350 --> 11:01.800
Sir, this line is reserved
for emergencies only.

11:01.850 --> 11:03.350
Please end your clammy joke.

11:03.390 --> 11:05.140
Okay. Sorry.

11:11.690 --> 11:14.520
- You remember what I told you?
- I'm the best around.

11:14.550 --> 11:16.320
Nothing's gonna ever keep me down.

11:16.340 --> 11:18.740
That's right. I made that up.
Now go get 'em, kiddo.

11:18.780 --> 11:20.740
I'll be watching with the other moms.

11:23.040 --> 11:25.290
Here's all the usual suspects.

11:25.330 --> 11:27.580
Oh, you're doing a video.

11:27.620 --> 11:31.040
Turn it... G-Get it off.
Glenn, I look terrible.

11:31.090 --> 11:33.090
Glenn, Courtney's up!

11:33.130 --> 11:35.380
Okay, okay, here we go. Please.

11:35.420 --> 11:37.180
Let's go, Courtney!

11:43.080 --> 11:45.420
Ah, perfect! That's a ten!

11:47.350 --> 11:50.560
9.2? 9.2?!

11:50.690 --> 11:52.540
9.2?!

11:55.490 --> 11:57.150
9.2?!

12:03.240 --> 12:06.630
9.2?! I'll give you a 9.2.

12:06.640 --> 12:08.200
On the Richter scale!

12:08.820 --> 12:10.330
Courtney, let's go.

12:10.380 --> 12:13.040
I get to go again. We do it twice.

12:13.090 --> 12:14.960
Oh.

12:28.360 --> 12:30.350
Let's go, Courtney.

12:33.190 --> 12:35.440
So, you liking Take Your
Daughter to Work Day?

12:35.460 --> 12:36.780
Uh, yeah!

12:36.800 --> 12:39.420
I can't believe my dad knows
how to fly this thing.

12:39.440 --> 12:42.600
- You want to try?
- Me? I don't know.

12:42.630 --> 12:43.779
Come on, it's easy.

12:43.780 --> 12:45.110
You don't even need a college degree,

12:45.120 --> 12:47.950
which is a very scary
true fact. Go ahead.

12:49.960 --> 12:51.800
You're doing great. Now roll it.

12:51.900 --> 12:54.000
What? No way.

12:54.010 --> 12:56.470
Don't worry, you're a Quagmire.
It's in your blood.

12:56.500 --> 12:58.420
- Grip it and rip it.
- Okay.

13:01.100 --> 13:02.880
Attagirl. Perfect.

13:04.060 --> 13:05.579
N-No. No, no. We're not doing that.

13:05.580 --> 13:07.680
I got my daughter with
me today, you perverts.

13:07.980 --> 13:09.700
He's not doing it today.

13:09.740 --> 13:11.100
- Aw, shoot.
- Another time.

13:11.120 --> 13:12.680
Probably got his kid with him.

13:16.540 --> 13:19.279
I'm glad you guys could
finally come over for dinner.

13:19.280 --> 13:21.100
Sure thing, Lois. Thanks for having us.

13:21.120 --> 13:23.800
See, Meg? That's a thigh gap.

13:23.840 --> 13:26.580
Now, Courtney, I'd like to
awkwardly introduce you

13:26.600 --> 13:27.840
to someone your own age.

13:27.890 --> 13:29.680
Courtney, this is Megan.

13:29.690 --> 13:31.519
Maybe you listen to the same music.

13:31.520 --> 13:32.540
- Hey.
- Hey.

13:32.560 --> 13:34.070
Yo, Courtney, what's your Instagram?

13:34.080 --> 13:35.979
I just got on there and
need some interesting peeps

13:35.980 --> 13:38.920
- to follow.
- Oh, you'll have to ask my dad.

13:38.930 --> 13:41.110
He approves all my follow requests.

13:41.120 --> 13:43.730
Denied! Nice try, ass.

13:43.780 --> 13:46.070
Hey, have you guys seen
the Wonder Woman film?

13:46.110 --> 13:48.110
- Yeah, no.
- Oh, you have to.

13:48.120 --> 13:49.440
It's a triumph.

13:49.470 --> 13:51.219
Courts and I have seen it five times.

13:51.220 --> 13:52.919
It's an important movie, Peter.

13:52.920 --> 13:55.340
You should watch it with
Meg. It's a masterwork.

13:55.380 --> 13:57.170
Oh, I've been wanting to see that.

13:57.210 --> 13:58.670
Okay, we totally will.

14:00.460 --> 14:02.350
Hey, Dad, I just checked the weather,

14:02.360 --> 14:04.760
and it looks like sunny
skies all weekend.

14:04.800 --> 14:06.420
You guys have big plans?

14:06.430 --> 14:07.720
Yeah, we're going camping.

14:07.750 --> 14:10.139
Hey, you and Meg should
come with us, Peter.

14:10.140 --> 14:12.300
We'll make it a father-daughter
bonding weekend.

14:12.320 --> 14:15.460
- Oh, that's a great idea.
- Yeah, let's go, Dad.

14:15.560 --> 14:17.680
Y-You know who you should
take instead of me?

14:17.720 --> 14:20.260
Uh, Stewie or-or Chris or Brian.

14:20.300 --> 14:21.600
May-Maybe Lois.

14:21.640 --> 14:23.760
Or Seamus is fun.

14:23.810 --> 14:26.019
Carter Pewterschmidt,
Babs Pewterschmidt,

14:26.020 --> 14:28.220
Bonnie, Joe, their son Kevin,

14:28.240 --> 14:31.000
Cleveland, Jerome, Bruce, Opie, Carl,

14:31.010 --> 14:33.850
the "phony" guy, the
ostrich, Al Harrington,

14:33.860 --> 14:37.190
Billy Finn, John Travolta
from one of our cutaways,

14:37.240 --> 14:40.340
uh, all of our characters
as Star Wars characters,

14:40.350 --> 14:42.099
everybody from The Cleveland Show,

14:42.100 --> 14:43.580
Cherry Chevapravatdumrong...

14:43.600 --> 14:44.910
that's how that name is pronounced...

14:44.950 --> 14:47.040
the Orville... the ship, not the cast...

14:47.080 --> 14:49.670
um, me... Aw, damn it!

14:49.710 --> 14:51.420
Okay, fine. I'll go.

14:51.460 --> 14:52.590
- Thank you.
- Cool.

14:52.630 --> 14:55.020
I heard my name, too. I'm in!

14:55.100 --> 14:57.840
No? I'll drive, buy snacks?

14:57.880 --> 14:59.720
No? Okay.

14:59.760 --> 15:01.760
Everyone else is out here, too.

15:10.190 --> 15:12.810
Oh, my God, it's literally everyone.

15:12.860 --> 15:15.680
That can only mean... show ghosts!

15:34.660 --> 15:37.460
_

15:39.800 --> 15:42.139
I'm really glad you decided to bring Meg

15:42.140 --> 15:43.219
on this camping trip, Peter.

15:43.220 --> 15:44.820
- It's gonna be great.
- Because we're in the...

15:44.840 --> 15:46.810
Because we're in the great outdoors.

15:49.310 --> 15:50.890
Ah.

15:50.940 --> 15:53.400
You don't get air like this
back in Quahog, do you, Pete?

15:53.440 --> 15:55.930
Uh, I don't know. Some places, probably.

15:55.940 --> 15:59.780
Hoo-ah! Gosh, being in nature
gives me such great energy.

15:59.820 --> 16:02.030
Hey, Courtney, you ever see
a yellow-headed warbler?

16:02.070 --> 16:04.370
That's the only warbler I haven't seen.

16:04.410 --> 16:05.950
Not for long it's not.

16:08.320 --> 16:11.520
Don't answer that. We're eating.

16:11.540 --> 16:12.599
They're probably eating.

16:12.600 --> 16:15.039
Okay, we're gonna have a
fun camp competition.

16:15.040 --> 16:17.580
And the first event, worth five points,

16:17.620 --> 16:19.300
is a race down to the lake right now!

16:19.340 --> 16:21.600
Last one there is a stinky poo-poo egg!

16:21.620 --> 16:22.660
Come on, Dad!

16:22.720 --> 16:26.510
What Meg didn't know,
what none of them knew,

16:26.560 --> 16:28.390
is that I already was

16:28.430 --> 16:30.770
a stinky poo-poo egg.

16:34.270 --> 16:36.500
Boy, you don't get stars like this

16:36.520 --> 16:37.770
back in Quahog, do you, Pete?

16:37.820 --> 16:39.070
Stop calling me Pete.

16:39.110 --> 16:41.650
I know what'll cheer you up. Skits!

16:41.700 --> 16:43.780
♪ Skits, skits, skits, skits ♪

16:43.820 --> 16:45.910
♪ Skits, skits, skits, skits ♪

16:45.950 --> 16:47.990
♪ Skits-skits-skits-skits, skits-skits ♪

16:48.040 --> 16:49.500
♪ Skits! ♪

16:53.740 --> 16:56.290
Well, isn't this a
perfect bench for a sit.

16:58.150 --> 17:00.730
Say, Dad, what are you doing?

17:00.770 --> 17:02.930
Oh, just sitting on the invisible bench,

17:02.940 --> 17:05.200
reading about those
North Korea jokesters.

17:05.210 --> 17:09.110
But, Dad, they moved the
invisible bench last week.

17:09.160 --> 17:11.070
Oh. It's over there now.

17:12.330 --> 17:14.080
Whoa!

17:17.120 --> 17:20.170
Ladies and gentlemen, "The
Invisible Bench" skit.

17:21.500 --> 17:22.680
Peter, you're up.

17:22.840 --> 17:25.940
Okay, here's one. I call
it "The Invisible Noose."

17:26.000 --> 17:28.130
First, I throw a rope
over this tree limb,

17:28.180 --> 17:29.630
put the noose around my neck.

17:29.680 --> 17:31.640
Now I'll just step onto this rock

17:31.660 --> 17:34.430
and jump off into the
sweet relief of death.

17:38.690 --> 17:41.440
Peter, would you mind
flattening your rod?

17:41.470 --> 17:43.900
Fine. I'll Tootsie it between my thighs.

17:43.940 --> 17:46.900
Yeah, okay, whatever gets it
away from my daughter's face.

17:52.410 --> 17:54.580
Are you eating an apple with a knife?

17:54.620 --> 17:56.450
God, that's always so forced.

17:56.500 --> 17:59.040
Hold on. We've been here already.

17:59.080 --> 18:00.910
Yeah, she's right.

18:00.960 --> 18:02.799
That's where I graffitied that rock.

18:02.800 --> 18:05.340
_

18:05.460 --> 18:08.170
We've changed our minds.
We're going on record.

18:08.220 --> 18:09.860
We're not lost, all right?

18:09.880 --> 18:11.880
We're just two dads bonding
with our daughters,

18:11.900 --> 18:13.680
and getting lost is
not part of the plan.

18:13.690 --> 18:14.709
All right, nobody panic.

18:14.710 --> 18:15.930
We just need to get our bearings.

18:15.970 --> 18:17.420
Hey, here comes a hiker.

18:17.440 --> 18:19.380
Excuse me, sir, we're lost.

18:19.390 --> 18:21.940
Ha! Then you must be my car keys, right?

18:21.980 --> 18:25.110
It is so nice to get out of the city

18:25.120 --> 18:26.570
and meet friendly people.

18:26.610 --> 18:29.140
You're not helping, Dad. As usual.

18:29.170 --> 18:30.740
Well, at least I didn't get us lost.

18:30.780 --> 18:34.380
We're not lost! We're just...
two dads in the woods,

18:34.390 --> 18:36.830
who love our daughters very, very much.

18:36.870 --> 18:39.540
Okay, so maybe it's not
the life we chose.

18:39.580 --> 18:42.139
Well, you chose it. I didn't.
That's for damn sure!

18:42.140 --> 18:43.670
- Dad, will you help him?
- Shh.

18:43.710 --> 18:45.580
I've been waiting for this.
I knew it was fake.

18:45.630 --> 18:47.340
Dad, I'm sorry. I didn't...

18:47.380 --> 18:49.460
I'm not Dad! I'm Quagmire!

18:49.510 --> 18:50.880
Glenn Quagmire!

18:50.930 --> 18:52.520
Giggity giggity!

18:52.550 --> 18:54.680
I don't want to be out
here! I hate camping!

18:54.690 --> 18:57.040
And what the hell was the
theme of that stupid prom?!

18:57.050 --> 18:58.960
All the cups said, "Oh, What a Night!"

18:58.980 --> 19:01.360
I mean, if it was, "Oh,
What a Knight" with a "K,"

19:01.380 --> 19:02.499
that would've made some sense,

19:02.500 --> 19:04.000
'cause there was a suit of armor there.

19:04.020 --> 19:05.940
What was that about? Answer me!

19:05.980 --> 19:08.960
I-I think it's possible to
overthink these things.

19:08.980 --> 19:10.400
Ugh, what a mish-mosh.

19:10.420 --> 19:12.030
Damn it, I just want to be home,

19:12.070 --> 19:14.980
not here, lost in the woods,
looking at this stupid map

19:15.000 --> 19:16.450
with a magnifying glass.

19:16.490 --> 19:17.620
Aah!

19:25.040 --> 19:27.660
Oh, my God. What are we gonna do?

19:27.670 --> 19:28.680
I don't know.

19:28.690 --> 19:31.200
- Help!
- Dear God, someone help us!

19:31.220 --> 19:33.090
You know when this would never happen?

19:33.130 --> 19:35.420
If I was sitting on the
couch, watching TV,

19:35.440 --> 19:37.060
ignoring you completely.

19:37.220 --> 19:40.470
Courtney, I'm sorry for
what I said earlier.

19:40.500 --> 19:43.060
You mean when you completely
ripped my school dance theme?

19:43.080 --> 19:44.940
No, no, there was no theme to rip.

19:44.960 --> 19:46.690
That's the point. I
stand by all of that.

19:46.730 --> 19:48.270
If anything, I'm more angry.

19:48.320 --> 19:50.470
No, I'm-I'm talking
about being your father

19:50.500 --> 19:51.780
before I was ready.

19:51.820 --> 19:54.570
I promise, if we make it out of here,

19:54.610 --> 19:56.320
we can start again.

19:56.370 --> 19:58.780
- Deal?
- Deal.

20:05.920 --> 20:07.500
9/11!

20:07.540 --> 20:09.710
Boston Strong!

20:09.750 --> 20:11.460
Oh, it's Smitty.

20:11.480 --> 20:12.800
We're saved!

20:12.840 --> 20:14.970
But we should warn the
birds the fire's coming.

20:16.800 --> 20:20.050
All right, stay calm.

20:20.100 --> 20:23.520
Grab the pictures. I'll
get your mother's ashes.

20:28.760 --> 20:31.900
Wow, Peter, that was a
close call with that fire,

20:31.910 --> 20:34.230
but I'm glad you all made
it back safe and sound.

20:34.280 --> 20:35.570
Yeah, me, too.

20:35.610 --> 20:36.950
What the hell?

20:36.990 --> 20:38.920
Oh, I hope it's okay.

20:38.930 --> 20:40.740
I bought some more pillows.

20:44.080 --> 20:47.300
I mean, what is the deal
with women and pillows?

20:47.320 --> 20:48.800
Has-has anyone else noticed this?

20:48.830 --> 20:50.500
No.

20:50.540 --> 20:51.660
No one?

20:51.670 --> 20:54.659
But I-I got three minutes
of material on pillows.

20:54.660 --> 20:56.540
We don't want to hear it.

21:03.010 --> 21:07.960
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv